course: dictionary
lesson: 10531
title: The udder
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An udder is the bag-like part that hangs under the belly of a female cow, goat or sheep. Milk is made there. Look for clues in the words around it: «A cow's udder has four quarters, each with its own milk gland and its own teat.» Four quarters means four parts, and each part has a teat, the nipple that milk comes out of.
explain: Milk comes out of the teats when a calf drinks, or when a farmer milks the animal. «Look under a cow at a dairy farm and you can count four teats, one for each quarter of the udder.» That is why a milking machine has four cups.
explain: Check a meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Many cows now walk into a milking robot all by themselves, because it means a tasty snack and a lighter udder.» A lighter udder means an udder with less milk in it, so the sentence makes sense.
fact: An udder is the bag-like part under the belly of a female cow, goat or sheep, where milk is made.
fact: «Udder» is a noun: one udder, two udders.
fact: Only female cattle give milk, from the udder.
fact: «Cow» means a female; males are bulls or bullocks, and the young are calves.
fact: A cow's udder has four teats; a goat or a sheep has two.
exercise: What is an udder? | The long woolly coat of a sheep | The horn on top of a bull's head | The pen where farmers keep hens | *The bag-like part under the belly of a female cow, goat or sheep, where milk is made
exercise: «A cow's udder has four quarters, each with its own teat.» How many teats does a cow's udder have? | Two | Six | One | *Four
exercise: «Only female cattle give milk, from the udder.» Which animals give milk? | Hens | Bullocks | Male bulls | *Female cows
test: Which animal's udder has two teats, according to the sentences? | Pig | Hen | Cow | *Goat
test: «Many cows now walk into a milking robot all by themselves, because it means a tasty snack and a lighter udder.» Why do cows walk into a milking robot? | To find a calf | To be painted | To go to sleep in the barn | *Because it means a tasty snack and a lighter udder
exam: Why does a milking machine have four cups? | Because four calves drink at the same time | *Because a cow has four teats, one for each quarter of the udder | Because it milks four farms at once | Because the farmer has four hands
